export anchor HackerIDEStyle:
    number: 293
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Hacker IDE
    idea: The pull request opens inside a modern dark code editor, with an activity bar, an explorer of repository views and changed files, editor tabs, a diff with change gutters and a minimap, a details panel, a checks terminal and a status bar.
    base: dark
    palette:
        editor: #0b0e13, the editor area, the diff and the terminal
        chrome: #151a21, the title bar, activity bar, explorer, details panel and style sheet cards
        tabRest: #1b212a, inactive editor tabs, chips, hover and the disabled merge button
        line: #262e3a, pane dividers and rows
        text: #d6dde8, text
        muted: #8f9bad, meta, line numbers, section headers and inactive tabs
        accent: #4fc1ff, the active tab top bar, the current view, links, the primary button and focus
        statusBar: #1f6feb, the status bar background behind white text
        green: #7ee787, passed, approved, Open, added lines and the add gutter
        red: #ff7b72, failing, removed lines and the remove gutter
        yellow: #e3b341, requested changes and strings
        purple: #d2a8ff, keywords and labels
        addTint: #12261b, added line rows
        delTint: #2d1517, removed line rows
    type:
        Interface text in system-ui, Segoe UI, Ubuntu, Roboto at 13px. The overview
        title 20px at 600. Explorer and panel headers 11px caps tracked 0.08em in
        muted. Code and terminal in JetBrains Mono, Fira Code, Cascadia Code,
        ui-monospace at 13px on 1.6. The status bar is 12px.
    layout:
        A full width editor window. A 36px title bar shows the branch, repository
        and app name with Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 at the right. Under it a grid
        of a 48px activity bar of icon buttons, a 260px explorer, the editor and a
        300px details panel. The explorer has a Repository section with the owner
        and name, Private, and the six tabs as views with counts, Pull requests
        current with an accent bar, and a Changed files tree with folders and the
        three files and their counts. The editor has a tab strip with Pull request
        214 and NotificationPrefs.tsx, the active tab marked by a 2px accent top
        bar. Under the tabs a breadcrumb, an overview block with the title, Open,
        the merge sentence, reviewers and labels, then the diff with old and new
        gutters, a coloured change bar, syntax colours, Tomás Ruiz's comment as an
        inline widget and a 64px minimap at the right. The details panel lists
        assignees, labels, milestone, linked issue and the disabled merge button. A
        bottom panel with Checks and Problems tabs prints the twelve checks as
        terminal lines. A 24px blue status bar shows the branch, the check score and
        the review state. Below 1100px the details panel moves under the editor,
        below 760px everything stacks and the activity bar turns into a row.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 22px tree rows, 35px tabs, 12px panel padding.
    density: Dense. A full workspace with many panes, small type.
    corners: Square panes and tabs, 4px buttons, fields and chips.
    borders:
        1px line dividers between every pane. A 2px accent top bar on the active tab
        and a 2px accent left bar on the current view. 3px gutter bars for added and
        removed lines.
    shadows: One shadow, under the inline comment widget, 0 4px 12px black at 50 percent.
    icons:
        Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke, 24px in the activity bar and 16px
        elsewhere. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
        triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge,
        always with the word.
    focus:
        A 1px accent outline offset negative 1px inside lists and tabs, and a 2px
        accent outline offset 2px on buttons and fields.
    tone:
        Tool voice, short and exact, such as CHANGED FILES, 11/12 checks and Merge
        blocked by 1 failing check.
